 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "**Where to look**\n\n- `src/tessel/app.py:1184-1190`: this is where the error is raised. `link_for` outside a request gets `url_adapter = self.build_url_binder(None)`, which returns `None` when there is no request.\n- `src/tessel/app.py:550-553`: `build_url_binder` only builds an adapter outside a request if `config[\"SERVER_NAME\"]` is set. The default at `app.py:215` is `None`, which is why the job crashes.\n- `src/tessel/helpers.py:200-244`: the `link_for` helper delegates to `active_app.link_for`, so it needs at least an app context.\n\n**Fix**\n\nSet these in the app config:\n\n```python\napp.config[\"SERVER_NAME\"] = \"example.com\"        # required\napp.config[\"APPLICATION_ROOT\"] = \"/\"             # as needed\napp.config[\"PREFERRED_URL_SCHEME\"] = \"https\"     # as needed\n```\n\nAlso make sure the job runs inside `with app.app_context():`. Outside a request, URLs are generated with the scheme and host from `SERVER_NAME`.",
